domain ADR0038:
  description "ADR-0038 revision 1: fragment commit and result reveal clocks. Status Proposed."

problem P1:
  |
    Proposed ADR-0037 records append-only fragments and provisional streaming
    but does not model prior-fragment memory, independent observation cuts,
    or the result-card display dependency. Accepted ADR-0006 still requires
    terminal-only public prose and receipt-keyed blocks. Accepted ADR-0016
    requires Beat-close narration jobs and one public block per Beat.

evidence OWNER_MODEL:
  |
    On 2026-09-29 the owner sketched Fragment N from prior Fragments and a
    Narrator observation, asked whether narrator memory is needed, and said
    Fragment boundaries need not follow Beat or Turn. After a chat model
    with committed observation and presentation-only memory was explained,
    the owner said OK and requested a new ADR to replace the older proposal.

evidence OWNER_PIPELINE:
  |
    The owner proposed ordered user-visible prose and speaker-labeled speech,
    required committed inputs plus successful generation and durable storage
    before Fragment commit, and identified retry at the blocked Fragment in
    the cumulative sequence. The owner then described provisional user
    Streaming as the meaningful speculative part of this pipeline.

evidence OWNER_REVEAL:
  |
    The owner wants canonical Battle computation to finish promptly and
    Narration generation to be the user-visible bottleneck. They selected
    result-card display only after the Fragment narrating the terminal
    outcome commits. They clarified that an earlier use of 'every' was a
    typo. They authorized recording the three clocks and result-card rule
    in a new ADR candidate, leaving terminal Narration failure unresolved.

evidence PRIOR_AUTHORITY:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0006 binds immutable narration input after canonical Battle
    commit, ordered delivery, terminal-only public prose, and public identity
    (battleId, turnReceiptId). It keeps Battle winner and state independent
    of narration. Accepted ADR-0016 creates jobs at Beat close and shows one
    public story block per Beat. ADR-0017 defines Turn and Beat clocks.

evidence CURRENT_WIRING:
  |
    On 2026-09-29 BattlePageView derived finished and the result panel from
    battle.status without a Narration reveal condition. This is current-code
    evidence only. The owner's historical repeated-display observation has
    not been independently reproduced and is not a premise of this decision.

premise SCOPE:
  |
    This is a new Proposed ADR candidate replacing the older Proposed
    ADR-0037 candidate. It does not accept itself, revise requirements or
    design documents, change code or Battle data, or apply a migration.
    Accepted ADR-0006 and ADR-0016 remain operative until a successor is
    accepted for their exact conflicting clauses.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Continue receipt-keyed terminal-only Beat blocks; couple Battle result
    display to immediate canonical status; or use independent committed
    Fragment coverage and a result reveal gate. The first two retain simpler
    current wiring but fail the owner's streaming, segmentation or reveal
    direction. The third requires source coverage and a presentation clock.

decision D1 based_on P1, OWNER_MODEL, OWNER_PIPELINE, PRIOR_AUTHORITY, OPTIONS:
  |
    Propose one logical Narration per Battle. Narration accumulates ordered
    immutable committed Fragments. A Fragment slot binds a fixed Narrator
    projection of committed canonical Battle evidence, selected earlier
    committed Fragments, the corresponding presentation-only narrator memory,
    and Battle-bound asset/style/policy revisions. Its cut is identified by
    canonical source coverage rather than defined by Beat or Turn boundaries;
    a cut may coincide with either. Exact cut criteria remain for basic design.

decision D2 based_on D1, OWNER_PIPELINE:
  |
    Propose attempt-scoped provisional Streaming from committed, frozen input.
    A completed and validated generation becomes a Fragment only after durable
    atomic storage of its ordered public content, source coverage and any
    narrator-memory transition. An attempt based on an uncommitted input
    cannot commit; internal speculative work, if later justified, does not
    publish prose or advance Fragment, memory or coverage. A failed attempt
    retains the prior committed prefix and retries the same blocked slot with
    the same bound input. A retry may generate different text and chunks.
    The prior ADR-0037 visible retry and terminal-failure display rules carry
    forward; exact retry count and exhaustion recovery remain open.

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, OWNER_REVEAL, PRIOR_AUTHORITY:
  |
    Propose three independent positions: canonical Battle commit, Narration
    Fragment commit, and user presentation reveal. Battle may reach a terminal
    result before Narration finishes. The result card is revealed once only
    when a committed Fragment references the terminal result and its validated
    content actually presents that outcome. Source coverage alone is not the
    reveal condition.
    Provisional Streaming may appear before its Fragment commits, but it does
    not release the result card. No Narration status or reveal state changes
    canonical winner, turn, Beat, rating or Battle events.

decision D4 based_on D1, D2, D3, PRIOR_AUTHORITY, SCOPE:
  |
    Propose replacing ADR-0006 terminal-only public prose and receipt-equals-
    public-block assumptions, and ADR-0016 Beat-close job/one-block-per-Beat
    presentation coupling, only after this ADR is explicitly Accepted.
    Retain ADR-0006 canonical-first commit, per-Battle ordering, durable
    outbox, finite authenticated reconnectable delivery, at-least-once event
    semantics and fencing. Retain ADR-0016/0017 Battle Beat and Turn clocks.
    The existing requirement candidate revision 1 predates the later owner
    decisions and must be reconciled in its own lifecycle before delivery.

pending OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    The product owner must review and explicitly accept, revise or reject
    exact ADR-0038 revision 1. This proposal does not alter Accepted
    ADR-0006 or ADR-0016 or authorize implementation or release.

pending TERMINAL_NARRATION_FAILURE:
  |
    If no Fragment covering the terminal result can be committed after
    retries, the rule for releasing the result card remains undecided. Do not
    invent a fallback Fragment, permanent hidden result or exception event.

pending CONTRACT_AND_APPLICATION:
  |
    Public Fragment identity and source-receipt mapping, exact cut policy,
    narrator-memory fields, other user-facing surfaces, existing Battle and
    client handling, and full-page provisional recovery require later owner
    or design decisions at their applicable phase.
